every project that i embark on  i put my heart and soul to do it and i  have a  very close relationship with the client  i listen  to their needs and understand what they  require from me  it is a space that i design not for me  but for the client  because it has to show the personality  of client it has to be a space  where they get happiness when they live  into the space and that is important to  me  i think my work no doubt i have projects  which are overseas projects but  it's very important to have a design  where it has to show that this design  actually has a singapore design identity  i have influence from the early  architects like le corbusier  mies van der rohe and oscar neva as well  as furniture designers  like charlotte parent search mole and  joe ponte  so this is obviously the early influence  that i have  in terms of how i understand design  it is important to understand especially  if you're doing interior design that  it has to relate to the external which  means we need to  respect the architecture we need to  understand the architecture  we need to understand back standard  spaces like the landscape  we need to understand how this element  has to be combined as a whole  my design style is modern classic and  luxe  modern in a sense that the design will  last over time  and what is what we call timeless design  classic which has a similar meaning is  that this design  will be carry over not just a decade but  in 20 in 30 years time and lux is about  using the material  inside the space so that the quality of  the space will be improved  through the selection of material  my advice to young designers is to be  passionate in whatever you do  to work hard and to strive for design  excellence  it's important to create a design that  is able to represent  singapore and this design will be  uniquely  singapore i'm peter tay interior  designer  designer  you
 

